## Notes on API Architecture

Before the blocks, key findings from the live docs:

- The AERONET Web Data Service v3 lives at `https://aeronet.gsfc.nasa.gov/cgi-bin/print_web_data_v3` and accepts mandatory parameters `year`, `month`, `day`, `AVG` (10 = all points, 20 = daily average), plus a data type flag (`AOD15=1`, etc.), with optional `lat1,lon1,lat2,lon2` bounding box in decimal degrees.

- IRSA's Gator catalog service (`https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/cgi-bin/Gator/nph-query`) supports cone searches against catalogs like `allwise_p3as_psd` and `fp_psc` (2MASS Point Source Catalog) via URL parameters `catalog`, `spatial`, `radius`, `radunits`, `outfmt`, and `selcols`.

- IRSA also exposes a VO TAP endpoint at `https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/TAP/sync` supporting ADQL queries with geometric constraints, covering catalogs including the 2MASS Point Source Catalog, with circle-based cone search.

- IRSA hosts public astrophysics catalogs from many missions including WISE/NEOWISE, 2MASS, ZTF, and more, all accessible without registration.

- For SDSS DR18, the SkyServer exposes a visual/REST navigation endpoint at `https://skyserver.sdss.org/dr18/VisualTools/explore/chartinfo` accepting `ra`, `dec` in degrees, and the SQL search API at `/dr18/SearchTools/sql` returns tabular data.

